| Topic | Link |
|-------|------|
| Next.js Docs | https://nextjs.org/docs |
| Tailwind CSS Docs | https://tailwindcss.com/docs |
| Redux Toolkit Docs | https://redux-toolkit.js.org/ |
| Stripe Checkout | https://stripe.com/docs/payments/checkout |
| Accessibility Audits | https://dequeuniversity.com/rules/a11y |
| Performance Budgeting | https://web.dev/performance-budget/ |

---

## TL;DR Checklist

1. **Initialize**: Vite + React + TS + Tailwind.  
2. **API layer**: Axios wrappers.  
3. **State**: Redux Toolkit slices for products & cart.  
4. **Pages**: ProductList, ProductDetail, Cart, Checkout.  
5. **Routing**: React Router with lazy loading.  
6. **Styling**: Tailwind utilities + dark mode.  
7. **Performance**: Code split, caching, service worker.  
8. **Accessibility**: Semantic tags, ARIA, contrast.  
9. **Testing**: Jest + RTL + Cypress.  
10. **Deploy**: Vercel/Netlify + env vars.

Follow this roadmap, tweak the stack to fit your team’s expertise, and you’ll have a scalable, maintainable e‑commerce frontend in no time. Happy coding!
